# Motivation, flow and states.
add(1568,'context','Emotional context in interaction','Why can recognizing the words in an utterance be insufficient for an appropriate social-robot response?', ['The same words can occur with different tone, context and expressed affect','A word transcript necessarily retains every acoustic property','An emotion label determines the exact semantic meaning without context','A speech recognizer directly measures the speaker’s internal feelings'], 'Words alone can omit cues relevant to how an utterance is expressed and interpreted.', ['A transcript usually loses pitch, timing and other acoustic detail.','A label does not replace semantic or situational context.','Speech recognition estimates words, not private feelings.'])
add(1569,'voice-flow','Voice assistant and robot-action branches','Which sequence follows the shown voice-assistant diagram?', ['STT → intent parsing → LLM, then TTS or ROS state machine → robot action','TTS → intent parsing → STT, then robot action → LLM','Robot action → TTS → intent parsing, with no speech input','LLM → microphone → ROS state machine → input transcript'], 'Speech is transcribed and interpreted before response generation, with speech and action output branches.', ['This reverses speech recognition and synthesis.','The diagram starts with user speech, not an action output.','The microphone supplies input rather than a post-LLM transcript.'],typ='diagram',kind='figure')
add(1570,'two-models','Human estimate versus robot state','What is the distinction between the human model and robot emotion state in this demonstration?', ['One estimates expressed human affect; the other controls the robot’s simulated response style','Both are direct measurements of the same human physiological state','The robot state is the raw microphone waveform and the human model is TTS','The human model stores motor torque while the robot state stores only word IDs'], 'The models have different subjects and roles, although the human estimate can influence the artificial robot state.', ['Neither description makes the state a direct physiological measurement.','Waveforms and synthesis are separate components.','These are not the two models’ roles.'])
add(1570,'simulation','Simulation versus consciousness','What does an internally maintained HAPPY state establish about Albert?', ['Its software has entered a named simulated state, not that it experiences happiness','The robot has acquired human consciousness','The user must also be happy','The state is a clinical measurement of the conversation partner'], 'The lecture explicitly describes simulation rather than evidence of subjective experience.', ['A state label does not establish consciousness.','The robot state need not copy the user estimate.','A software state is not a clinical measurement.'])
add(1571,'state-parts','States, triggers, transitions and actions','A frustration cue causes a robot to change from neutral to supportive and soften its voice; which mapping is correct?', ['Cue: trigger; neutral→supportive: transition; soft voice: output action','Cue: output; soft voice: trigger; neutral→supportive: stored sensor image','Cue: transition; neutral→supportive: input microphone; soft voice: state identifier','All three are the same state with no transition'], 'A trigger activates a state transition, whose resulting state can select an expressive action.', ['This reverses the input trigger and output action.','A transition is a change between states, not the microphone.','The scenario explicitly includes a state change.'],typ='scenario')
add(1571,'state-dependence','Transition inputs','Which information can affect transitions in the described emotion state machine?', ['User interaction, context and internal variables','Only the final display color, never interaction','Only a fixed lecture slide number','Only the vocabulary size of the language model'], 'The state-machine description includes external interaction and context as well as internal variables.', ['The listed transition causes are broader than display output.','A lecture page number is not a state input.','Vocabulary size is not the stated trigger set.'])
